{"id": "section-body-14698", "title": "Uveitis", "chapterId": "chapter-fourteen", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "EYE DISEASES AND REFRACTIVE ERRORS", "Painful Red Eyes", "Uveitis"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-14698", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Uveitis", "runs": [{"text": "Uveitis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1271"}}, {"id": "body-14699", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "This is Inflammation of the uveal tissue (Iris, choroid and ciliary body) and its adjacent structures. Majority of the cases are idiopathic whereby other cases are due to autoimmune diseases e.g. Rheumatoid Arthritis, Sarcoidosis, SLE ocular or systemic infections e.g. Viral, Tuberculosis, Leprosy, and Syphilis.", "runs": [{"text": "This is Inflammation of the uveal tissue (Iris, choroid and ciliary body) and its adjacent structures. Majority of the cases are idiopathic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "whereby"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "autoimmune"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diseases"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "e.g."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Rheumatoid"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Arthritis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Sarcoidosis,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "SLE"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ocular"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "systemic infections e.g. Viral, Tuberculosis, Leprosy, and Syphilis."}]}, {"id": "body-14701", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-14702", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It has three main Clinical Presentations namely acute, chronic and acute on chronic. The commonest form is anterior uveitis. In acute type, patients present with: -"